WEBVTT

00:00:00.119 --> 00:00:00.786
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.785
Phrasal verbs

00:00:03.722 --> 00:00:05.396
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1, D

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.535
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘Dig in’ means start to eat.

00:00:10.416 --> 00:00:12.244
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2, H

00:00:12.927 --> 00:00:15.232
<v><b>F:</b></v> ‘Eat up’ means eat all of something.

00:00:17.247 --> 00:00:19.012
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3, C

00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:24.218
<v><b>F:</b></v> ‘Pick at’ means take small amounts or bites because you are not hungry.

00:00:26.163 --> 00:00:27.841
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4, A

00:00:28.618 --> 00:00:32.179
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘Polish off’ means finish the last items of food or drink.

00:00:34.147 --> 00:00:35.866
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5, E

00:00:36.596 --> 00:00:39.948
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘Put away’ means consume large quantities of something.

00:00:41.724 --> 00:00:43.595
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6, G

00:00:44.341 --> 00:00:48.520
<v><b>F:</b></v> ‘Toy with’ means play with something and move it round carelessly.

00:00:50.377 --> 00:00:52.297
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7, B

00:00:53.058 --> 00:00:56.186
<v><b>M:</b></v> ‘Tuck into’ means eat food with enthusiasm.

00:00:58.064 --> 00:00:59.778
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8, F

00:01:00.572 --> 00:01:05.214
<v><b>F:</b></v> ‘Wolf down’ means eat in a hurry by putting a lot of food in your mouth at once.